---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../data/site";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy | Morium" description="How Morium collects, uses, and protects your data.">
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-8">
		<a href="/" class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent-700 hover:text-accent-800">&larr; Back to Morium</a>
		<h1 class="mt-6 font-display text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink/60">Last updated October 19, 2026</p>

		<div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink/75">
			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Who this covers</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					Morium is booking, customer, and invoicing software for mobile service
					businesses. This policy covers this website, the Morium app, and the
					booking pages and websites we run for businesses. It speaks to two
					groups of people: the business owners and teams who use Morium, and the
					customers of those businesses.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-2">
					Morium is operated by Brock Livermore, doing business as Morium. You can reach us, and send any
					legal notice, at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="font-semibold text-accent-700 hover:text-accent-800">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">What we collect</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					<strong class="text-ink">From you, as a business owner or team member:</strong>{" "}
					your business name, email, and password (our login provider stores the
					password only in scrambled form, never in a form anyone can read), your
					plan and payment status, and what you enter to set up your business:
					services, prices, hours, a logo and photos, your Google review link,
					and the names, emails, and roles of the people on your team.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-3">
					<strong class="text-ink">About your customers:</strong> what you enter,
					and what a customer types into your booking form: name, phone number,
					email, service address, vehicle, notes, the service and time they want,
					how they heard about your business, and their booking and invoice
					history. If you use before and after photos (Crew plan), those are
					stored too. That data belongs to your business, not to us.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-3">
					<strong class="text-ink">Activity log:</strong> Morium records who in
					your business changed something important (a price, a payment, a role)
					and when. Your owners can see it.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-3">
					<strong class="text-ink">Technical information:</strong> our servers and hosting providers keep
					standard logs (the page asked for, the time, and the IP address), and we
					use IP addresses briefly to slow down abuse, such as a script flooding a
					booking form. We do not use advertising or analytics trackers on
					morium.one or in the app.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-3">
					<strong class="text-ink">Website waitlist:</strong> If you join our website waitlist on morium.one, we collect the name, business name, email address, and optional phone number you enter, only to contact you when websites open up, and we use Cloudflare Turnstile on that form to block bots.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">How we use it</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					We use your data to run the service you signed up for: showing your
					bookings dashboard, taking bookings, sending the emails you've turned
					on, creating invoices and pay links, processing your subscription
					payment, keeping the service secure, and contacting you about your
					account. We don't sell your data or your customers' data to anyone, for
					any reason.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Who we share it with</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">The companies below make Morium work. We share data with them only for that, and with nobody else:</p>
				<ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
					<li><strong class="text-ink">Stripe</strong> handles your subscription payment. We never see or store your card number.</li>
					<li><strong class="text-ink">Stripe, for card payments from your customers.</strong> To take card payments you connect a Stripe account through Morium. Your customer pays on a Stripe page, and the money goes to your own Stripe account, not to us. Stripe collects the identity and bank details it needs to verify you, under its own terms. Morium keeps the invoice amounts and Stripe's reference numbers, never card numbers.</li>
					<li><strong class="text-ink">Supabase</strong> hosts the database, the login system, and file storage (logos, gallery photos, and vehicle photos), in the United States.</li>
					<li><strong class="text-ink">Railway</strong> runs the Morium app, in the United States.</li>
					<li><strong class="text-ink">Vercel</strong> hosts this marketing website.</li>
					<li><strong class="text-ink">Resend</strong> delivers every email Morium sends: review requests, rebook reminders, booking confirmations, appointment reminders, invoices and pay links, owner alerts, team invites, and password resets. Resend sees the recipient's address and the message.</li>
					<li><strong class="text-ink">Google.</strong> If a business turns on Google reviews, each visit to its homepage makes our server ask Google for that business's public reviews. We do not keep them. The review text, names, and photos come from Google, and reviewer photos load from Google's servers. Every page of the Morium app, including the login and signup pages and the dashboard, loads its fonts from Google Fonts, and so do the websites and booking pages we run. Google receives the visitor's IP address when one of those pages loads. This marketing website does not use Google Fonts.</li>
					<li><strong class="text-ink">Push notification services.</strong> If you turn on push notifications, they are delivered through your browser's or phone's push service (and Expo's, for the mobile app).</li>
					<li><strong class="text-ink">Calendly.</strong> If you book a call with us about the website add-on, Calendly handles that booking under its own policy.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Emails and opting out</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">Morium sends two kinds of email for a business, and they are treated differently:</p>
				<ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
					<li>
						<strong class="text-ink">Review requests and rebook reminders</strong> are marketing
						emails. Only these carry an unsubscribe link (plus the business's
						mailing address). Anyone who clicks it stops getting these emails from that business.
						Our sending system checks the opt-out before every one and skips anyone who
						unsubscribed. The business chooses whether each kind goes out automatically or only after
						the owner approves it.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="text-ink">Booking confirmations, reschedule and cancellation notices, quote
						received emails, price changes, appointment reminders, and invoices and pay links</strong> are
						transactional emails: they are about a booking or a payment the customer made. They have no
						unsubscribe link, and they still go to a customer who unsubscribed from marketing emails.
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="mt-3">
					Morium does not send text messages. The "text" buttons in the app open your own Messages
					app with the words filled in. You press Send, and it goes from your own number.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Cookies and storage</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					Morium sets a cookie to keep you signed in. The websites and booking pages we run remember a
					visitor's light or dark choice on their own device. We use no advertising or tracking cookies.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-3">
					<strong class="text-ink">Do Not Track.</strong> We don't track you across other websites or online
					services. Because of that, a "Do Not Track" setting in your browser changes nothing about how we
					handle your information.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">If you are a customer of a business that uses Morium</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					We hold your information on that business's behalf. To see, correct, or delete what a business
					has about you, ask the business. You can also email us at{" "}
					<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="font-semibold text-accent-700 hover:text-accent-800">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>{" "}
					and we'll pass your request on. To stop a business's review requests and rebook reminders, use the
					unsubscribe link in the email.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">How we protect it</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					Everything travels over secure connections (HTTPS). Each business can only see its own records, and
					the database itself enforces that, not just the app. No system is perfect, so tell us right away at{" "}
					<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="font-semibold text-accent-700 hover:text-accent-800">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>{" "}
					if you think someone got into your account.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Your copy, and deleting your data</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					In the app, owners can download the bookings and the customers as spreadsheets. When your
					subscription ends, we keep your business's data so you can come back where you left off. We do not
					delete it automatically. To have it deleted, email us at{" "}
					<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="font-semibold text-accent-700 hover:text-accent-800">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>{" "}
					at any time and we'll delete your business's data, including your customers' records, from our
					systems. Copies in
					our backups can take a little longer to disappear. Stripe and
					Resend keep their own records under their own rules. For example, Stripe keeps payment records it is
					required to keep.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Changes to this policy</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					When we change this policy, we update the date at the top. If the change is a meaningful one, we
					plan to email the account owners as well.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Questions</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="font-semibold text-accent-700 hover:text-accent-800">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> and a real person will answer.
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>
